lor:black">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; System restart.<o:p></o:p></span>=
</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" align=3D"left" style=3D"text-align:left"><span lang=
=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;co=
lor:black"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" align=3D"left" style=3D"text-align:left"><span lang=
=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;co=
lor:black"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" align=3D"left" style=3D"text-align:left"><span lang=
=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;co=
lor:black">I think the correct behavior should be :<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" align=3D"left" style=3D"text-align:left"><span lang=
=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;co=
lor:black">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return -EINVAL;<o:p></o:p></span>=
</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" align=3D"left" style=3D"text-align:left"><span lang=
=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;co=
lor:black">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tell user not a typewriter.<o:p><=
/o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" align=3D"left" style=3D"text-align:left"><span lang=
=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;co=
lor:black"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" align=3D"left" style=3D"text-align:left"><span lang=
=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;co=
lor:black">Analysis of causes:<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" align=3D"left" style=3D"text-align:left"><span lang=
=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;co=
lor:black">In the process of using the PPP device driver, if the unit of th=
e PPP device file has been created. On the basis of the
 above, the ioctl function is used to pass the PPPIOCSMAXCID command and th=
e 0x67084000&nbsp; parameter (parameters must be satisfied: arg&gt;&gt;16 &=
gt; 255 and 0xFFFF&amp;arg &gt; 255), which will lead to the use of null po=
inters in the kernel.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" align=3D"left" style=3D"text-align:left"><span lang=
=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;co=
lor:black">The null pointer is used specifically in the slhc_init function,=
 and the function is defined as follows:<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" align=3D"left" style=3D"text-align:left"><span lang=
=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;co=
lor:black">////////////////////////////slhc_init///////////////////////////=
////////////<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" align=3D"left" style=3D"text-align:left"><span lang=
=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;co=
lor:black">struct slcompress *<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" align=3D"left" style=3D"text-align:left"><span lang=
=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;co=
lor:black">slhc_init(int rslots, int tslots)<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" align=3D"left" style=3D"text-align:left"><span lang=
=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;co=
lor:black">{<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" align=3D"left" style=3D"text-align:left"><span lang=
